; MXFS — SELinux labeling rule for the mxfs filesystem type
;
; A distribution policy has no rule for a filesystem type it has never heard
; of, so without this every file on an MXFS mount is unlabeled_t, and a
; confined service (libvirt's sVirt QEMU, httpd, containers) is denied it.
; MXFS stores labels in security.* extended attributes and labels a new inode
; through security_inode_init_security, exactly as XFS does, so it takes the
; rule the reference policy gives xfs: fs_use_xattr with fs_t for the
; filesystem object itself.
;
; Installed by the RPM's %post with semodule -i; a mount made before the
; module was loaded keeps its old labeling until it is remounted.

(fsuse xattr mxfs (system_u object_r fs_t ((s0) (s0))))
